A||||2||Greg Piet||exterior door handle||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||09-06-2000||02:49 PM||||What entails fixing the door handle...  I think there are quite a few people out there who know what I am referring to...<BR>One side wobbles as if it is broken...<BR>Is replacement difficult?  Getting in the door from the inside is pretty tight over there(I replaced a lock assembly from the inside and it was a bear).||||reg||1
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-06-2000||02:58 PM||||I believe it's pretty easy to unbolt the handle from the inside, maybe only two nuts or bolts.  You will need to take the door pad off, roll the window up, etc.  You'll need to rotate the nylon clip that connects the handle to the linkage and the handle should come out.  Sounds like the little spring behind the handle is bad, you might be able to fix it once you get it off the car, but it might be just easier to find a good one from the boneyard.  Hope this helps...<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-06-2000||06:27 PM||||If the handle's loose, it's either broken or about to break.  It's not that hard to change handles (I've done 4 or 5 so far.)  Like Hugggggggggggr said, you need to remove the inner door panel and roll the window up.  Then remove the linkage (you'll see what I mean once you take a look) and the two speed nuts (they're on the two studs on the back of the handle assy).  You'll need to lift the handle (just the handle, not the entire assy), then pull straight out.  One or both of the studs might be a little tight.  Just wiggle them and they'll come out.  The installation is the reverse.  The toughest part is getting the linkage reconnected.  If you have any questions, feel free to email me.||||reg||1
